## UI Consistency Rule (Mandatory)

When building or modifying any page or component, you must match the existing design system exactly:

- **Primary color:** Deep purple (used for headings, active nav, titles)
- **Accent color:** Gold/yellow (used for buttons, highlights, underlines)
- **Background:** Light gray page background, white card/container surfaces
- **Typography:** Bold dark headings, small gray subtitles below page titles
- **Layout:** Every page must have a centered title + subtitle header block at the top, followed by the main content card
- **Cards:** White background, soft box shadow, rounded corners
- **Buttons:** Gold background, white bold text, rounded, full-width or right-aligned
- **Spacing:** Consistent padding inside cards, no excessive empty space
- **Nav:** Active nav item uses deep purple with an underline

Before writing any JSX, reference the existing pages (`Dashboard.jsx`, `StudentHistory.jsx`) as the visual baseline. Your output must be visually consistent with those pages — a developer should not be able to tell which page was AI-generated.

Never launch browser subagents or perform automated visual testing. The developer will handle all testing manually.